    {
      "id": "claim_7632ee0dd86b49168649f0d55262823f",
      "statement": "The No service URL workflow triggers on push and pull_request targeting main, and its job greps all src/environments/*.ts files for a non-empty apiUrl; any match fails the job with instructions to set apiUrl back to ''.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/no-service-url.yml#L16-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e783bcdd04b85e7cb311463df18cb9bb399ee2f745fa06e4ebb0cf6728b5ab99:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ddbf76032b0448e2a5049b893a81ed17",
      "statement": "The empty-apiUrl check is gated at the job level by `if: github.repository == 'ulabase/starter-vue'`, so forks and copies with a different repository name register the trigger but skip the check entirely — by design, because `ulabase setup` writes a real service URL that fork owners are expected to commit to their own app.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/no-service-url.yml#L16-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1e629c1b9cbb3090e2a09c6fc442eebf9ee0d5f38fe7dd0ddc33bfc60f1fe24a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4c596402da574dceabbe4efa22c4f1fc",
      "statement": "In this repository, `apiUrl` in src/environments/environment.ts is committed as an empty string; running `ulabase setup --srv <srvId>` fills it in as a local, uncommitted change, and pushing that change to main is what the No service URL workflow exists to prevent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/no-service-url.yml#L1-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7be837cbb4f85eb75d6d6c6682d98973e77fc647eed926c6ae75d8d81c65bde6:"
