        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4eeb1c7a813b41ce895e74df90214179",
      "statement": "The OpenWiki Update workflow runs on a nightly cron at 03:00 UTC, on pushes of semver tags matching [0-9]+.[0-9]+.[0-9]+, and on manual workflow_dispatch with an optional `message` input that is passed to openwiki as a run-specific instruction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L5-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b9089f19b3979ac4f7c93854799db1b6e665889ce52e573f565e5ccf5a64144:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b21684fab4c7499a97b954a0c381c2ff",
      "statement": "Scheduled OpenWiki runs perform change detection against the last commit that touched openwiki/, diffing to HEAD while excluding openwiki/, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md; the run proceeds only if at least one source file changed, whereas tag and manual dispatches always proceed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L40-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7bc5d0e3d46a2ed3037230a42fb5a5b58eaf55cc4da39b4e9d1b9dc2263c80d4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_883620c266394bb88ef40d0ddf813564",
      "statement": "The workflow selects its mode by filesystem state: `--init` when no openwiki/ directory exists yet (first generation), `--update` for incremental regeneration otherwise; the optional manual message is appended via --print as an instruction for that run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L64-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d2d096cd1cdb0c0a618bdbed8eadf3a8b432b26d74059971fc35d20c2ebc7d0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1944822008884ed9bf7ef3894a46b131",
      "statement": "The workflow always checks out `main` (even when triggered by a release tag) with full history, because a tag checkout is a detached HEAD from which no pull request can be opened and the wiki describes main.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L30-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:50686e7f9be1a2b8762b26209ddc4bb9856acee5d6267dbfe9225f5cb156ce5e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0d8f31f58f1c4240aa3d712d365c9e5c",
      "statement": "A concurrency group (openwiki-update, cancel-in-progress: false) serializes runs so overlapping executions wait rather than cancel; the created PR on the openwiki/update branch is auto-merged with `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch --auto`, falling back to a plain merge, which requires 'Allow auto-merge' to be enabled on the repository.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L22-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b5128337484d378a11aaf08aebe2a5a395c7c36614ed7b4626c44a8a44083f7:"
